# Use `@apply` in Component CSS Files

When writing CSS in `src/css/**/*.css`, use Tailwind's `@apply` directive to express properties that map to utilities. Raw CSS property declarations are only acceptable when no utility exists.

## Rules

- **Always `@apply`**: colours (`text-*`, `bg-*`, `border-*`), font family (`font-main`, etc.), layout (`flex`, `grid`, `overflow-*`), spacing that maps to the scale (`p-*`, `m-*`, `gap-*`), cursor, opacity, z-index, transforms
- **Keep raw CSS**: `color-mix()` values, non-standard sizes that require arbitrary values (e.g. `0.6875rem`), `transition` with specific durations and properties, `!important` rules
- **Scrollbars (Tailwind 4.3+)**: use `scrollbar-thin`, `scrollbar-thumb-*`, and `scrollbar-track-*` in `@apply` (theme colours e.g. `scrollbar-thumb-border-soft`); not raw `scrollbar-width` / `scrollbar-color`

## Examples

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
.my-block {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-body);
    overflow: hidden;
}

/* ✅ GOOD */
.my-block {
    @apply flex items-center bg-(--color-surface) text-(--color-body) overflow-hidden;
}
```

```css
/* ✅ OK — raw CSS only for what @apply cannot express */
.my-block {
    @apply flex cursor-pointer font-main text-(--color-body) uppercase;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;        /* no matching Tailwind token */
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;      /* non-standard tracking */
    transition: color 150ms;    /* specific duration */
}
```

## Responsive variants in `@apply`

Use arbitrary breakpoints inline instead of separate `@media` blocks:

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
.my-col { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-soft); }
@media (min-width: 800px) { .my-col { border-bottom: none; border-right: ...; } }

/* ✅ GOOD */
.my-col {
    @apply border-b border-(--color-border-soft) min-[800px]:border-b-0 min-[800px]:border-r;
}
```
